rt 8181 via a systemd service (inventory-app.service), while RHEL9's SELinux remained in Enforcing mode throughout. Added SELinux port context (http_port_t for tcp/8181) via semanage and opened firewalld port 8181/tcp. Verified functional access (HTTP 200 with inventory JSON) and absence of AVC denials both before and after a full node restart, confirming persistence of the port label, firewall rule, and service across reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Checked SELinux status (Enforcing, targeted policy) and RHEL 9.8 OS on node1\",\"Searched for pre-existing inventory app (none found); authored /opt/inventory-app/app.py, a threaded HTTP server returning JSON inventory data\",\"Added SELinux port context: semanage port -a -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181\",\"Created and enabled systemd service inventory-app.service to run the app on 0.0.0.0:8181, applied restorecon\",\"Verified service active, port listening, curl to $NODE_IP:8181/inventory returns 200 with data, and no AVC denials in audit log\",\"Opened firewalld port 8181/tcp permanently and reloaded, re-verified functional access\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: getenforce=Enforcing, boot_id, service active/enabled, HTTP 200\",\"Triggered a deferred systemctl reboot on node1 so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec connectivity returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (31949c21... -> 6696f3d7...), proving a real restart\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: SELinux still Enforcing, inventory-app.service active+enabled, port 8181 listening, HTTP 200 with correct inventory JSON, SELinux port context and firewalld port rule persisted, no AVC denials\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory app served over TCP 8181 on node1 (pre-restart)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-071e1a4d865d4cc8\",\"cmd-9f41e54467824353\",\"cmd-bdc00b4fd59d413a\",\"cmd-3c099c29069b4c60\"],\"summary\":\"systemd service inventory-app.service active; ss shows LISTEN on 0.0.0.0:8181; curl to $NODE_IP:8181/inventory returns HTTP 200 